UK-WHO-0-2y-2026.08.07
Task R2. UK-WHO LMS reference table, both sexes, weight/length/head-circumference,
birth to 2 years (age_days 0-730).

Source repository: https://github.com/rcpch/growth-references
Source file:        uk-who/UK_WHO_0_20_preterm.csv
Commit:              c13ee6983f94cb4c74f257bf70a62958cd5e3bc4 (main, 2025-07-27)
Retrieved:           2026-08-07

Composition (per SPEC D4 / 5.1): rows tagged "British1990" in the source file
for age_days 0 and 7 (40-41 weeks gestation columns; the source also carries a
week-42/day-14 British1990 row and a preterm gestational-tracking extension
back to 23 weeks gestation - both dropped here, since day 14 onward is WHO2006
per spec and this table only serves postnatal lookups, never gestational-age
lookups). Rows tagged "WHO2006" for age_days 14-730. Where the source carries
a duplicate point at exactly age_days=730 (WHO publishes separate LMS sets for
recumbent length, 0-2y, vs standing height, 2-5y, with a small measurement-
convention discontinuity at the boundary), the 0-2y/recumbent-length row was
kept and the 2-5y/standing-height row dropped, since this table's scope is
birth->2y only.

Units: source weight is kg (converted x1000 to grams), source length/head-
circumference are cm (converted x10 to millimetres), matching this table's
grams/millimetres convention (see reference/lms.py). L and S are dimensionless
and were not rescaled.

